  "_note": "Northern pike (Esox lucius), a rare ambush hunter of weedy Midwest lakes. Markings from field-guide descriptions: long and torpedo-shaped with a flat duck-bill snout, dark green with rows of LIGHT bean-shaped spots, a cream belly, the dorsal and anal fins far back by the tail, and reddish fins with dark marks. From above, as seen from a boat, the shape is exaggerated: a flat duck-bill snout narrower than the head, the dorsal and anal fins showing near the tail. The dorsal and anal fins are solid wedges and the tail a lens, so they show from above too. 650 mm long, the base length (SECOND-ORDER R1.150-R1.169).",
